{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass when they see, etc.</b> He prefaced by telling her the reason for what he commands her immediately afterward — <b>say now, please</b>, etc. — that she should say it from the start and announce it without being asked anything, that she should make an effort to make it known that she is his sister. And His saying <b>say now, please</b> means: now, without being asked. Now, since one might ask why it is necessary to announce anything without being asked, therefore he said: because otherwise there will be no question, and when they see them they will know from the circumstance that she is his wife. And it is His saying <b>and it shall come to pass when they see</b>, etc. — they will not ask anything, for on their own they will say: she is surely his wife. And since they say this in their mind, they will kill Abraham — therefore he preempted by sending forth a voice of brotherhood to everyone who recognizes and sees them."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:54.038291948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}